Unscoped Anonymous Task Data:
Because existing tasks lack a userId, blindly attaching a backend or requiring a login could cause existing local user tasks to become inaccessible or mistakenly overwritten.
Account Switching / Local Cache Leakage:
When User A logs out and User B logs in on the same browser or Android device, the application must completely isolate each user's tasks. User B must never see User A's cached tasks, completion remarks, or private notes.
Data Loss During Account Deletion:
Deleting an account must only delete cloud and local records owned by that specific authenticated user. It must never clear anonymous data belonging to other device profiles.
Offline First & Synchronization Races:
Chronos operates offline-first. Introducing authentication must not break offline task creation or editing when disconnected from the network.
Database Migration Safety:
Android's Room schema must be migrated from version 2 to 3 using a non-destructive migration (ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN userId TEXT DEFAULT NULL) to prevent data wipe.
